<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Audio on 0x32++</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/audio/</link><description>Recent content in Audio on 0x32++</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 13 Jan 2009 16:11:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/audio/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Dial Up Modem, sound no longer heard?</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/dial-up-modem-sound-no-longer-heard/</link><pubDate>Tue, 13 Jan 2009 16:11:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/dial-up-modem-sound-no-longer-heard/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;One sound you don&amp;rsquo;t hear very often these days, you&amp;rsquo;d to be something of a comforting sound back in the early days of the interwebs. Maybe its like a white noise machine or something.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;object width="425" height="344"&gt;&lt;param name="movie" value="http://www.youtube.com/v/eKOUEpQ8pRY&amp;hl=en&amp;fs=1"&gt;&lt;/param&gt;&lt;param name="allowFullScreen" value="true"&gt;&lt;/param&gt;&lt;param name="allowscriptaccess" value="always"&gt;&lt;/param&gt;&lt;embed src="http://www.youtube.com/v/eKOUEpQ8pRY&amp;hl=en&amp;fs=1" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" allowscriptaccess="always" allowfullscreen="true" width="425" height="344"&gt;&lt;/embed&gt;&lt;/object&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle&amp;rsquo;s Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>10 of the Best Songbird Add-ons</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/10-of-best-songbird-add-ons/</link><pubDate>Fri, 05 Dec 2008 12:01:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/10-of-best-songbird-add-ons/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;s