Qh5yzDI77uBMIba5UmVrkOR0gmw/s1600-h/pot-o-gold.jpg" target="Bwindow"&gt;&lt;img style="margin: 0px 10px 10px 0px; float: left; cursor: pointer; width: 217px; height: 320px;" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEg7b463u8IjTSmajUK1CRyI3HWUj2tNheMi7B31KO4LaX8aNmoGiM_42xRBQk-6WLBp-QMGN0KXmSS-aaFDB252XvZm3n4Uw-At-hrPulHcqdQfyYh2Qh5yzDI77uBMIba5UmVrkOR0gmw/s320/pot-o-gold.jpg" alt="" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>In Car MP3 Player</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/in-car-mp3-player/</link><pubDate>Tue, 11 Nov 2008 08:03:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/in-car-mp3-player/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a onblur="try {parent.deselectBloggerImageGracefully();} catch(e) {}" href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEh-r29fbP-Dofm1t9W_uLMO7GM1saBSta5s7iS_UN4ksNFEDax-4r9herjC2SuY_bGvHa5hY5DRcA3B_oYNXvNl8awKOx1Q7LLXt1ZFRXf8gRpmcGKrkhMSL2PGQaYvyDew6K2_vSHzZZM/s1600-h/DSC00489.JPG"&gt;&lt;img style="float:left; margin:0 10px 10px 0;cursor:pointer; cursor:hand;width: 299px; height: 400px;" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEh-r29fbP-Dofm1t9W_uLMO7GM1saBSta5s7iS_UN4ksNFEDax-4r9herjC2SuY_bGvHa5hY5DRcA3B_oYNXvNl8awKOx1Q7LLXt1ZFRXf8gRpmcGKrkhMSL2PGQaYvyDew6K2_vSHzZZM/s400/DSC00489.JPG" border="0" alt="" id="BLOGGER_PHOTO_ID_5267307777629765042" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Got myself an in car MP3 player, you can either plug in the iPod etc or a USB drive or SD card with your tracks on it, which it then plays through the car&amp;rsquo;s radio.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;a href="http://tinyurl.com/6fuord"&gt;In-Car 12v MP3 FM Modulator&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="http://tinyurl.com/5k3nwx"&gt;Memory2Go Orbit 360 2GB USB2.0 Flash Drive&lt;/a&gt; combined to make the drive to and from work more bearable.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Not bad for £17 including postage.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle&amp;rsquo;s Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>MediaMonkey</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/mediamonkey/</link><pubDate>Wed, 08 Oct 2008 08:26:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/mediamonkey/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 5 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 8 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.bloglines.com/"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;I found the intelligent tag editor really useful. &lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;a name="base13329014"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a name="base13329014"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;div id="items13329014" style="display: block;"&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr bgcolor="#ffffff"&gt; &lt;td&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;h2&gt;&lt;a title="Site: FileHippo.com" href="http://www.filehippo.com/download_mediamonkey/4750/"&gt;MediaMonkey 3.0.5.1187&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img style="float: left; margin-right: 5px;" src="http://i.filehippo.com/img/ex/1128__mediaMonkey2.gif" /&gt;MediaMonkey is a music manager and jukebox for serious music collectors and iPod users. It catalogs your CDs, OGG, WMA, MPC, FLAC, APE, WAV and MP3 audio files. It offers an intelligent tag editor which looks up missing Album Art and track information&amp;hellip;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>VLC 0.9 Revamps Interface, Playlist Features [Featured Download]</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/bloglines-vlc-09-revamps-interface/</link><pubDate>Mon, 29 Sep 2008 15:18:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/bloglines-vlc-09-revamps-interface/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 17 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 21 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.bloglines.com/"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;One for the download list &lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;a name="base1105048"&gt; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;table id="table1105048" bgcolor="#bde0ed" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt; &lt;td rowspan="2"&gt; &lt;table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align="left" valign="top"&gt; &lt;a href="http://lifehacker.com/"&gt;&lt;img src="http://cache.gawker.com/assets/base/img/thumbs140x140/lifehacker.com.png" alt="Lifehacker" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;br /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;span class="blogtitle"&gt;&lt;a href="http://lifehacker.com/"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Lifehacker&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Computers make us more productive. Yeah, right. Lifehacker recommends the software downloads and web sites that actually save time. Don&amp;rsquo;t live to geek; geek to live. &lt;/td&gt; &lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;a name="base1105048"&gt; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;div id="items1105048" style="display: block;"&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr bgcolor="#ffffff"&gt; &lt;td&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;h2&gt;&lt;a title="Site: Lifehacker" href="http://feeds.gawker.com/%7Er/lifehacker/full/%7E3/406277252/vlc-09-revamps-interface-playlist-features"&gt;VLC 0.9 Revamps Interface, Playlist Features [Featured Download] &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; By Kevin Purdy on Windows &lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Convert &amp;amp; Extract Audio from Videos</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/convert-extract-audio-from-videos/</link><pubDate>Sun, 28 Sep 2008 11:31:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/convert-extract-audio-from-videos/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 20 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 30 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Music from video &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;a name="base9477167"&gt; &lt;table id="table9477167" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="5" bg style="color:#bde0ed;"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt; &lt;td rowspan="2"&gt; &lt;table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;span class="blogtitle"&gt;&lt;a href="http://pipes.yahoo.com/pipes/pipe.info?_id=8IsQFi282xG5FaTJJjBjOg"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Life GH Com&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Pipes Output &lt;/td&gt; &lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;div id="items9477167" style="display:block; position:block;"&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr bgcolor="#ffffff"&gt; &lt;td&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;h2&gt;&lt;a title="Site: Life GH Com" href="http://feeds.cybernetnews.com/~r/CyberNet/~3/vGYOSP4FGcg/"&gt;Convert &amp;amp; Extract Audio from Videos&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://feedads.googleadservices.com/~a/Tbj75J7Ci64pZWERl-vOKbilTNM/a"&gt;&lt;img src="http://feedads.googleadservices.com/~a/Tbj75J7Ci64pZWERl-vOKbilTNM/i" border="0" ismap="ismap" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://cybernetnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/pazera.png" class="highslide"&gt;&lt;img src="http://cybernetnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/pazera-tm.jpg" width="450" height="337" alt="pazera.png" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;em&gt;(Click to Enlarge)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;There have been a few times where I've wanted to extract audio from video files, but it's not always easy to find a free tool that can successfully do that. I highly recommend grabbing the &lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://www.pazera-software.com/products/audio-extractor/"&gt;free Pazera app&lt;/a&gt; if you ever find yourself in a similar situation. To make it even more useful the program also doubles as an audio conversion utility.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>